      <tr><td class="px" style="padding:0 56px;">
        <p class="body" style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:16px;color:#5b5147;line-height:1.9;">Pavillon Rouge du Château Margaux took its name in 1908. After an eclipse from the 1930s to the mid-1970s, production resumed under André Mentzelopoulos in 1977; from the mid-1990s, the creation of a third wine allowed an ever more rigorous selection. Today its quality stands very close to the Grand Vin — sharing its flavours, its balance and the same subtle interplay of power and softness.</p>
        <p class="body" style="margin:0;font-size:16px;color:#5b5147;line-height:1.9;"><span class="sans" style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#a6864e;text-transform:uppercase;">The 2025 Vintage&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;</span>Born of a particularly rigorous selection — just 28% of the harvest was chosen for Pavillon Rouge 2025. A blend led by 70% Cabernet Sauvignon and raised in 60% new oak, it is long and beautifully fresh, with a little more emphasis on powerful tannins than the Grand Vin.</p>
      </td></tr>

